// Deployment configuration (copied to the build as-is — edit it after
// deploying the dist, no rebuild needed):
//
//   window.__FM_CONFIG__ = { base: '/path/to/app/' }
//
// `base` is the public path of the app (must end with a slash): the app
// derives the router base, the API URL (<base>/../api) and the docs URL
// (<base>/../docs) from it. The built-in default below fits the standard
// /app/ deployment (the node's random_url_path is empty).
//
// deploy.sh rewrites both this file and the static <base> in index.html from
// the node's random_url_path. When editing manually, set `base` here and, if
// the app is NOT mounted in an "app" directory, the <base> href in index.html
// too. On deep links the value here also wins over the path recovered from
// the URL ("…/app/…").
window.__FM_CONFIG__ = { base: '/app/' }
